      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: The `static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e` casts can be omitted, because the `uint16_t` type is still promoted to `int` by C++\u0027s integral promotion.\n\nNote: The following is effectively what actually happens:\n\n```\n  const uint16_t value \u003d (int)static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(reader-\u003edata[0]) |\n                         (int)static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e((int)reader-\u003edata[1] \u003c\u003c 8);\n```\n\nNote the three `(int)` casts that I added to indicate where integral promotion occurs.",
      "revId": "d4265e8385b8cbe48c38173b671b4ff9b3f843c3",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
